; A rate stated in a currency that is not the transaction's.
;
; 100 USD bought with 15,000 yen, each leg quoted off the statement it came
; from: the USD leg against CAD, the yen leg against the USD it bought. The
; entry is denominated in CAD — the first rate names it — and the yen leg's
; rate is per USD.
;
; Applied as though every rate were in the transaction's currency, the yen
; leg was valued at 15,000 × 0.0066… = 100.00 CAD instead of the 135.00 CAD
; it is worth, GnuCash balanced the 35.00 difference by inventing an
; Imbalance, and the run reported success. Nothing in the file was wrong: the
; rate was read as answering a question it was not asked.
;
; This tool's own export always quotes in the transaction's currency, so only
; a hand-edit produces it.
;
; What this fixture produces: a refusal naming the posting, the currency its
; rate is in, and the one the entry is denominated in.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
    gnucash-mnemonic: "CAD"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Canadian Dollar"
    gnucash-fraction: "100"
